    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0386" n="312" xml:id="pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-06">January 6,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the
                    President</hi>:</p>
                <p>The attached is a telegram which Churchill proposes to send to the Dutch apropos
                    of their complaints about the agreement.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d179-f1"/></p>
                <p>I gave it to Stark and he consulted Marshall, King and Arnold and they find the
                    telegram is all right.</p>
                <p>Immediately following the draft telegram is a memorandum of explanation which
                    Stark drafted.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d179-f2"/> I don’t quite understand it but
                    the main thing is that your staff recommend that the cable go as dictated.</p>
                <p>If it has your approval I will give it to the British and they will get it off
                        tonight.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d179-f3"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry L. Hopkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d179-f1" n="1" xml:id="d179-f1-content">
                <p>The attached telegram was a copy of Churchill’s draft telegram of January 5,
                    1942, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg305">p. 305</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d179-f2" n="2" xml:id="d179-f2-content">
                <p>The attachment was a copy of Stark’s letter to Hopkins, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d179-f3" n="3" xml:id="d179-f3-content">
                <p>The memorandum was returned with the handwritten notation: “H.L.H.—OK FDR”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
